---
import NotebookLayout from "~/layouts/NotebookLayout.astro";
import NotebookPage from "~/components/NotebookPage.astro";
import CodeCell from "~/components/CodeCell.astro";
import Polaroid from "~/components/Polaroid.astro";
import Sticky from "~/components/Sticky.astro";
import Prose from "~/components/Prose.astro";
import Marker from "~/components/Marker.astro";
import CodeInline from "~/components/CodeInline.astro";
import FileTree from "~/components/FileTree.astro";
import { findLesson } from "~/lib/lessons";
import { open, close, a, kw, ident, punct, expr, str, tag, comment, attr, string } from "~/lib/hl";

const lesson = findLesson("02-add-some-markdown")!;

const mdCode = `${punct("---")}
${attr("title")}${punct(":")} ${str("Launch day")}
${attr("date")}${punct(":")} ${str("2026-10-14")}
${attr("author")}${punct(":")} ${str("Mae Jemison")}
${punct("---")}

${kw("##")} What happened

Ignition at <strong>T-0</strong>. Apollo 42 cleared the tower in <em>8 seconds</em>.

The booster sep was on the nose. Mission Control breathed a long, deep breath.`;

const pageCode = `${kw("---")}
${kw("import")} ${ident("Layout")} ${kw("from")} ${str("\"~/layouts/Layout.astro\"")}${punct(";")}

${comment("// markdown files are real ES modules.")}
${comment("// frontmatter is exported as &#96;frontmatter&#96;.")}
${kw("import")} ${punct("{")} ${ident("frontmatter")}${punct(",")} ${ident("Content")} ${punct("}")} ${kw("from")} ${str("\"~/content/logs/launch-day.md\"")}${punct(";")}
${kw("---")}

${punct("&lt;")}${tag("Layout")}${a("title", "Launch day")}${punct("&gt;")}
&nbsp;&nbsp;${open("article")}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${open("h1")}${expr(`${ident("frontmatter")}${punct(".")}${ident("title")}`)}${close("h1")}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${open("p", a("class", "byline"))}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${expr(`${ident("frontmatter")}${punct(".")}${ident("author")}`)} · ${expr(`${ident("frontmatter")}${punct(".")}${ident("date")}`)}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${close("p")}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${punct("&lt;")}${tag("Content")} ${punct("/&gt;")}
&nbsp;&nbsp;${close("article")}
${punct("&lt;/")}${tag("Layout")}${punct("&gt;")}`;
---

<NotebookLayout title={lesson.title}>
    <NotebookPage lesson={lesson}>
        <Prose>
            <p>So far you've written HTML in <CodeInline>.astro</CodeInline> files. Fine for buttons. <Marker>Awful for prose.</Marker></p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p>For posts you want <Marker color="pink">Markdown</Marker>. Headings with <CodeInline>##</CodeInline>, italics with underscores, links in brackets. Astro reads <CodeInline>.md</CodeInline> files natively.</p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p>Drop the post in a new <CodeInline>src/content/logs/</CodeInline> folder:</p>
        </Prose>

        <CodeCell file="src/content/logs/launch-day.md" note="Markdown file" code={mdCode} />

        <Prose class="mt-4">
            <p>Then a regular Astro page <CodeInline color="red">imports</CodeInline> it. Markdown files give you two things: <CodeInline highlight>frontmatter</CodeInline> (the YAML on top, as data) and <CodeInline highlight>Content</CodeInline> (a component that renders the body).</p>
        </Prose>

        <CodeCell file="src/pages/logs/launch-day.astro" highlightLine={5} code={pageCode} />

        <Prose class="mt-4">
            <p>Visit <CodeInline>/logs/launch-day</CodeInline>. The Markdown renders as proper HTML — paragraphs, headings, the lot. <Marker color="pink">Writing > coding</Marker> for content.</p>
        </Prose>

        <Fragment slot="pinboard">
            <Polaroid caption="page 2 ✦ /logs/launch-day" rotate={2}>
                <div class="bg-white border border-ink-dark/15 rounded-md font-[system-ui]">
                    <div class="bg-paper-warm px-3 py-2 border-b border-ink-dark/10 text-[11px] font-bold text-ink-dark">
                        🛰 Mission Control
                    </div>
                    <div class="px-3 py-3">
                        <h2 class="text-[20px] font-bold mb-1 text-ink-dark leading-tight">Launch day</h2>
                        <p class="text-[10px] text-ink-soft mb-2">Mae Jemison · 2026-10-14</p>
                        <h3 class="text-[13px] font-bold mb-1 mt-2 text-ink-dark">What happened</h3>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-dark/90 leading-snug">
                            Ignition at <strong>T-0</strong>. Apollo 42 cleared the tower in <em>8 seconds</em>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 font-sketch text-sm text-pen-green italic">prose from markdown.</p>
            </Polaroid>

            <FileTree
                title="src/"
                rotate={-2}
                root={{
                    name: "src",
                    children: [
                        {
                            name: "content/",
                            isNew: true,
                            children: [
                                {
                                    name: "logs/",
                                    isNew: true,
                                    children: [{ name: "launch-day.md", isNew: true }],
                                },
                            ],
                        },
                        {
                            name: "pages/",
                            children: [
                                { name: "index.astro" },
                                {
                                    name: "logs/",
                                    isNew: true,
                                    children: [{ name: "launch-day.astro", isNew: true }],
                                },
                            ],
                        },
                    ],
                }}
            />

            <Sticky color="yellow" rotate={1.5}>
                <h3 class="font-title text-[26px] text-ink-dark leading-none mb-2">Already free:</h3>
                <ul class="font-hand text-[16px] text-ink-dark/90 space-y-1 leading-tight">
                    <li>· <CodeInline>**bold**</CodeInline>, <CodeInline>*italic*</CodeInline></li>
                    <li>· <CodeInline>[links](url)</CodeInline></li>
                    <li>· headings, lists, blockquotes</li>
                    <li>· fenced code blocks with highlighting</li>
                    <li>· tables, images, footnotes</li>
                </ul>
            </Sticky>

            <Sticky color="mint" rotate={-1.5}>
                <h3 class="font-title text-[24px] text-ink-dark leading-none mb-1">Try this</h3>
                <p class="font-hand text-[16px] text-ink-dark/90 leading-tight">
                    Add a fenced code block to your <CodeInline>.md</CodeInline>. Astro highlights it for free — same Shiki you get in your IDE.
                </p>
            </Sticky>
        </Fragment>
    </NotebookPage>
</NotebookLayout>
